WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.969
-My next guest
is an Emmy-nominated performer

00:00:03.969 --> 00:00:05.771
who you know
from "Saturday Night Live."

00:00:05.771 --> 00:00:09.242
She also stars in the new show
"Schmigadoon,"

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:12.545
which premieres this Friday
on Apple TV+.

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:16.782
Everyone, please welcome back
Cecily Strong!

00:00:16.782 --> 00:00:18.418
-♪ Cecily Strong ♪

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:20.686
♪ She knows how to jive ♪

00:00:20.686 --> 00:00:22.388
♪ She is the woman ♪

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:24.790
♪ From "Saturday Night Live" ♪

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:26.493
Cecily Strong

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:28.961
♪ Coming at you soon ♪

00:00:28.961 --> 00:00:30.396
♪ Hope she's explanin' ♪

00:00:30.396 --> 00:00:34.366
♪ What is a Schmigadoon ♪

00:00:34.366 --> 00:00:35.802
-Cecily Strong!

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:37.603
That's a --
That's a standing ovation.

00:00:37.603 --> 00:00:39.772
-Oh, that's sweet!
-They love you.

00:00:39.772 --> 00:00:41.207
Come on.
-How nice.

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:42.608
-They love you. I love you, too.

00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:44.210
Thank you for
coming on the show,

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:45.911
but thank you for doing
a sketch with us.

00:00:45.911 --> 00:00:47.246
-Oh, it's so much fun.

00:00:47.246 --> 00:00:49.248
You know I love to sing
and dance with you, Jimmy.

00:00:49.248 --> 00:00:51.484
-I know.
We always have fun doing it.

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:53.953
I got to say the Emmys
were announced,

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.989
and you got your second
Emmy nomination.

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:59.325
Congratulations.
Well-deserved.

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:01.727
-Thanks. It was very nice.

00:01:01.727 --> 00:01:04.998
And it feels like it was a good
celebration, I got to share

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:07.566
with a lot of my cast mates
who were making history.

00:01:07.566 --> 00:01:09.401
I mean, Aidy Kenan
got the double.

00:01:09.401 --> 00:01:11.771
-Oh, that's right.
Aidy Bryant. Kenan Thompson.

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:12.972
That's right.
-And Bowen.

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:14.907
-And Bowen Yang.
-First time a feature player.

00:01:14.907 --> 00:01:16.475
-I always want to call you
on a Sunday.

00:01:16.475 --> 00:01:17.910
Thank God
I don't have your number.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:19.912
'Cause I just want to be like --
Or text you and say,

00:01:19.912 --> 00:01:22.214
"That was the funniest thing
you've ever done."

00:01:22.214 --> 00:01:23.716
-I've given you
some fake numbers.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:25.618
-Yes, you actually have.
You and Don Cheadle.

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:26.752
-For that purpose.

00:01:26.752 --> 00:01:28.354
Yeah, no one gives me
their real number.

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:31.424
But you do -- And every week,
you top yourself.

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:33.159
And you crush it every week.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:34.560
And, you know,
everyone loves you.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.796
But, dude, Jeanine Pirro?

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:39.866
-It's very fun.
And she loves me the most.

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:42.735
-But you going into
the giant box of wine.

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:44.537
-Yeah.
-Singing "My Way"

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:47.506
and just whipping wine
at Colin Jost.

00:01:47.506 --> 00:01:49.375
-Why not?
Colin loves it more than anyone.

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:50.910
I've never seen
anything like it.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.778
-You know what's great?
It looks like it's so much fun

00:01:52.778 --> 00:01:54.080
that you're having out there.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:55.581
That's the secret
to the whole thing.

00:01:55.581 --> 00:01:59.018
-I mean, and it's like you can
tell them, "Fine, if I'm going

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:00.352
to do Pirro again, I need to..."

00:02:00.352 --> 00:02:01.854
"Well, I barfed wine last time,

00:02:01.854 --> 00:02:03.656
so I should get in a tub of wine
this time."

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:05.592
-You'll top yourself.
-And then they're like --

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:07.927
Richie's like,
"Okay, we'll figure it out."

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:09.395
-Yeah, Richie.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:11.230
And then, I mean,
even, like, the safety guy

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:13.332
at some point said to me
beforehand -- He was like,

00:02:13.332 --> 00:02:17.070
"Okay, I've tested getting
into the grapefruit juice."

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:19.438
And I kept going,
"Why grapefruit juice?

00:02:19.438 --> 00:02:20.973
What does that even look like?"

00:02:20.973 --> 00:02:23.209
I think it was grape juice.
So that was a weird thing.

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:25.377
-That's sticks in your head?
-"Have you been throwing

00:02:25.377 --> 00:02:27.513
grapefruit juice in your eyes?"
And he kept saying,

00:02:27.513 --> 00:02:29.448
"Don't open your eyes
in the grapefruit juice.

00:02:29.448 --> 00:02:31.484
It stings."
And I was like,

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:33.786
"What do you think
I'm going to be doing in this?"

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:36.355
-Yeah.
-In the tub like...

00:02:36.355 --> 00:02:37.656
"Shape of Water."

00:02:37.656 --> 00:02:39.125
-Just jumping in
and dunking quick.

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:40.859
-I don't know
that you had to throw

00:02:40.859 --> 00:02:42.695
grapefruit juice in your eyes.
-It was a good warning

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:44.130
from him,
but you crushed it either way.

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.865
I want to talk
about "Schmigadoon."

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:48.134
I've heard about this.
I knew it going into production.

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:49.602
I was like,
"Oh, this is gonna be..."

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:51.971
You. Keegan-Michael Key.
-I love it so much.

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:54.807
-Dude, the production
on this thing is insanity.

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:56.408
-Yes, yeah.

00:02:56.408 --> 00:02:58.545
-Can you set it up in a
couple lines or what it's about?

00:02:58.545 --> 00:03:00.346
-Sure. I think so. I hope so.
-Yeah.

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:02.815
-It's a couple that is kind of

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:04.484
at a stale point
in their relationship.

00:03:04.484 --> 00:03:05.851
They're doctors,

00:03:05.851 --> 00:03:08.054
and they go on a hike,
as one does, to fix it.

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:09.522
-Yeah.

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:12.958
-And they get lost in a town
that turns out to be a musical.

00:03:12.958 --> 00:03:14.927
And they can't leave
until they find true love,

00:03:14.927 --> 00:03:17.129
which is strange to hear
if you think you're in love.

00:03:17.129 --> 00:03:18.998
-That's what I'm talking about.
I love that.

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:21.334
They're stuck in this town.
-Yeah.

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:25.138
-And, by the way,
some heavy hitters in this.

00:03:25.138 --> 00:03:27.873
Alan Cumming. Kristin Chenoweth.

00:03:27.873 --> 00:03:29.709
-Yes.
-She -- How powerful --

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:31.077
-She's unreal.

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:33.112
I feel like she made
a quotable line

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:34.580
out of every line she had.
-Yeah.

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:36.315
-She was just like,
"Oh, yes, you do!"

00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:38.451
Just does -- And I was like,
"Wow. That's how --

00:03:38.451 --> 00:03:40.085
You can, 'Yes, thank you.'"

00:03:40.085 --> 00:03:42.188
Or just, "Ahem."
-Yeah, just a --

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:44.256
-I guess no one says "Ahem."
-No one does "Ahem."

00:03:44.256 --> 00:03:46.492
-That's how it's written,
but that's not how you say it.

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:49.395
-[ Clears throat ]
-Ahem!

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:50.863
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:03:50.863 --> 00:03:52.998
Here's Cecily Strong
in "Schmigadoon."

00:03:52.998 --> 00:03:54.367
Take a look at this.

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:56.902
-So, you have a feller?

00:03:56.902 --> 00:03:58.905
-Y-Yes, I have a feller.

00:03:58.905 --> 00:04:01.673
-And he's okay with you
walking on your own at night,

00:04:01.673 --> 00:04:03.843
talking with strange men?

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:06.812
-Well, he's...

00:04:06.812 --> 00:04:09.015
What's the question again?

00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:10.916
-Wait a minute.
What are you trying to do?

00:04:10.916 --> 00:04:12.851
Are you trying to get me
to fall for you?!

00:04:12.851 --> 00:04:14.953
-What? No.
-Well, then why do those

00:04:14.953 --> 00:04:17.790
crazy kind of thoughts
keep running through my head?

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.659
-Oh, I don't really --
-Well, you can forget it.

00:04:20.659 --> 00:04:23.963
Because no woman is gonna tie
Danny Bailey down, no how.

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:25.330
-Sure.

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:28.467
-♪ When a squirrel
wants another squirrel ♪

00:04:28.467 --> 00:04:31.070
♪ He don't bother
to get attached ♪

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:33.873
-Oh, I get a private show.

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:35.107
-Come on!
-That was me.

00:04:35.107 --> 00:04:37.143
-You know how to do it
right there!

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:40.946
Cecily Strong, everybody!
Oh, you're one of my favorites.

00:04:40.946 --> 00:04:42.548
Come back whenever, buddy.

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:45.585
"Schmigadoon" is streaming
on Apple TV+ this Friday.

